   "record": "92d97340bcdd0d9a0281793ed9121272b293aeaec37e52e028571fd523a9ff23",
   "status": "MISMATCH",
   "ruling": "Ruling: scope; project retained. i1040sd p. 15, line 1: \"Enter your taxable income from Form 1040, 1040-SR, or 1040-NR, line 15. (However, if you are filing Form 2555 (relating to foreign earned income), enter instead the amount from line 3 of the Foreign Earned Income Tax Worksheet in the instructions for Form 1040, line 16.)\". The Form 2555 alternative is never reached on a return the tool computes: the exclusion is reported on Schedule 1, line 8d (i1040gi p. 91: \"Foreign earned income exclusion and housing exclusion from Form 2555\"), refused by s1.line8_other (forms/2025/s1.yaml: \"lines 8a, 8d, 8e, 8k to 8q and 8s to 8v are refused by s1.line8_other\"); the housing deduction (Schedule 1, line 24j) is refused at Form 1040 line 10 (\"lines 24b to 24z are outside this tool\"); and a filer who answers that Form 2555 is filed is refused at Schedule 1-A line 2a (forms/2025/s1a.yaml, gate sa.excluded_income, i1040gi p. 101). The worksheet note records Form 2555 as outside scope. The restatement says what the page says for every return the tool computes; as round 2. No change.",
   "subject_key": "a236c2e48aba00c6f7d83802c6a16875609c61dde9512e9a9e3c096f0cb81e17"
  },
  {
   "key": "2",
   "record": "33c23102d78a20c4ddb59685ca4085cd7b07af14df68c246ed0ee0352424bcf3",
   "status": "MISMATCH",
   "ruling": "Ruling: model error; i1040gi p. 25, Line 3a: \"Qualified dividends are also included in the ordinary dividend total required to be shown on line 3b\", and line 3b is box 1a of the Forms 1099-DIV (with substitute statements and dividends received without a form, as the box 1a question asks), so no qualified dividend exists with box 1a at zero.",
   "subject_key": "f943de91a7d109ac26fd386838e789b878e01d3e8ce6f70daaa8b84a970ac45e"
  },
